    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to individual student needs, providing instant feedback on problems, and explaining concepts in simple terms. For example, they can generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level or clarify confusing topics. This makes math more engaging and reduces anxiety for students."
